! Water wB97X / STO-3G: ANALYTIC-Hessian frequencies  (v0.88.2)
!
! Phase-3 exercise: the closed-shell analytic Hessian of a range-
! separated hybrid.  Every layer carries the -rs_beta*K_lr blocks:
! the 2e skeleton runs a second, erf-attenuated exchange-only pass
! (second-derivative integrals through the same vrr seeds as the SCF
! and gradient operators); the derivative Fock gains -rs_beta*dK_lr;
! all batched CPKS response builds add -rs_beta*K_lr[dP].
!
! Reference values (1 thread, default grid; bit-reproducibility
! references -- see the grid note in test_v088_h2o_wb97x.inp):
!
!   SCF total energy:   -75.312832162016 Ha   (deliberately
!                        distorted geometry, NOT a minimum)
!   Frequencies:  1941.70 / 3968.68 / 4269.62 cm^-1
!
! Cross-validation (v0.88.2 battery): the NUMERICAL Hessian (central
! differences of analytic gradients, with the geometry-fingerprinted
! attenuated store) gives 1937.49 / 3974.61 / 4275.01 cm^-1 on the
! same input; the two Hessian matrices agree to 2.2e-3 Ha/bohr^2 max
! element -- the same level both routes show at the omega -> 0 limit,
! i.e. the long-range blocks are exact.  B3LYP baseline on the same
! geometry: 17 / 1 / 0.6 cm^-1 between the two routes.
%method  WB97X
%basis   sto-3g
%job     freq
%hess_method analytical
%charge  0
%mult    1
%geom angstrom
O    0.000000    0.000000    0.135000
H    0.000000    0.780000   -0.480000
H    0.000000   -0.780000   -0.480000
*end
